Fixed-value flags need only prefix filtering over a tiny tuple.  The helper
stays generic so the shared module-level option objects and the command-local
[[--fence]] and [[--render]] options can all advertise the same accepted values
without repeating the list comprehension.

<<functions>>=
def _choice_completer(values: tuple[str, ...]):
    def _complete(_ctx: typer.Context, incomplete: str) -> list[str]:
        return [value for value in values if value.startswith(incomplete)]

    return _complete
@

The command-local [[--fence]] and [[--render]] options can pass
[[autocompletion=_choice_completer(...)]] directly to [[typer.Option(...)]],
because their construction happens inside [[<<cli setup>>]] -- by then both
the choices and the helper are defined.  The shared module-level options
above sit in [[<<constants>>]], which is tangled before [[<<functions>>]],
so [[_choice_completer]] does not yet exist when they are constructed.  We
therefore wire their completion callbacks here, in a chunk that runs after
both definitions are in scope.  The contract test below pins this wiring so
a future refactor that drops the assignments, reorders the top-level chunks,
or upgrades to a Typer release that rejects attribute mutation fails loudly
instead of silently leaving tab-completion empty.

<<option completions>>=
LAYOUT_OPTION.autocompletion = _choice_completer(LAYOUT_CHOICES)
QR_FORMAT_OPTION.autocompletion = _choice_completer(QR_FORMAT_CHOICES)
EXPORT_FORMAT_OPTION.autocompletion = _choice_completer(EXPORT_FORMAT_CHOICES)
PIN_HEAT_OPTION.autocompletion = _choice_completer(PIN_HEAT_CHOICES)
RESULTS_WINDOW_OPTION.autocompletion = _choice_completer(RESULTS_WINDOWS)
@

<<test functions>>=
@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "option, expected",
    [
        (LAYOUT_OPTION, LAYOUT_CHOICES),
        (QR_FORMAT_OPTION, QR_FORMAT_CHOICES),
        (EXPORT_FORMAT_OPTION, EXPORT_FORMAT_CHOICES),
        (PIN_HEAT_OPTION, PIN_HEAT_CHOICES),
        (RESULTS_WINDOW_OPTION, RESULTS_WINDOWS),
    ],
)
def test_shared_options_advertise_choice_completion(option, expected):
    completer = option.autocompletion
    assert completer is not None
    assert completer(None, "") == list(expected)
@

