<<functions>>=
def _tutorial_dir() -> Path:
    return Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "tutorials"


def _tutorial_paths() -> tuple[Path, ...]:
    tutorial_dir = _tutorial_dir()
    return tuple(tutorial_dir / name for name in TUTORIAL_FILENAMES)

@

The presenter-only routes normally trust the loopback address, but that trust is
unsound behind an SSH reverse tunnel: the tunnel forwards remote visitors to
[[localhost]] on the serving machine, so every public request appears to come
from [[127.0.0.1]].  UPnP does not have this problem---it forwards a port while
preserving the real client address---so only the SSH mode replaces localhost
trust with an unguessable per-run token.  Generating the token here, in the
mode-aware CLI, keeps the server itself agnostic about how exposure happens.

<<functions>>=
def _admin_token_policy(public: PublicMode) -> tuple[Optional[str], bool]:
    require_token = public is PublicMode.ssh
    token = secrets.token_urlsafe(16) if require_token else None
    return token, require_token
@

The public-serving branch has start-up lines of its own.  It runs
inside the shared URL context above, rewrites remembered QR targets
when the public URL changes, and announces that URL.  When the tunnel
disables localhost trust it prints the tokenised admin link instead of
the plain index hint, because the bare index URL would now be refused
for the lecturer too.  The lines are returned, not printed: the caller
decides when and how often they are shown (\cref{sec:server-runners}).

<<functions>>=
def _public_start_lines(
    store: Store,
    host: str,
    port: int,
    public_url: str,
    *,
    results: bool,
    lock: bool,
    admin_token: str | None,
) -> list[str]:
    count = regenerate_qrs(store, public_url)
    lines = [_address_line(f"Public URL: {public_url}", count)]
    if admin_token is not None:
        lines.append(
            "Presenter admin link (keep private; localhost trust is "
            "disabled behind the tunnel):\n"
            f"  {public_url}/?admin={admin_token}"
        )
    elif not results:
        lines.append(_format_index_hint(public_url, host, port))
    if lock:
        lines.append(_format_lock_hint(public_url))
    return lines
@

