\subsection{Open-question fence option}

The optional [[--fence]] flag keeps the CLI and LaTeX helper in sync.  A
lecturer can say [[--fence python]] when the question expects a code upload,
and uploaded files will later be wrapped in a Markdown fence on the results
page so the renderer emits a language-tagged [[<code class="language-...">]]
block.

Like the other render subcommands, [[open]] only has to build the question,
delegate the real formatting work, and persist the metadata that later layers
use.  The CLI test therefore only needs to verify that [[--fence]] reaches the
stored [[OpenQuestion]].

