A restart moves the session window forward while the watcher runs, so
the window holds fewer answers than the watcher has already printed.
An answer arriving after the restart is still new and must appear,
numbered within the new window, and the count printed with it names
its window as the heading does, so the drop reads as a new session.
An answer from before the first start is outside the window from the
first frame on.

