The admin index is admin only for a request from the loopback address,
unless the token makes it so.  A server bound to a loopback address or
to every interface is reached through loopback; the test binds
[[127.0.0.2]], a loopback address other than the usual one, and the
real server must answer the opened URL with the index.  A server bound
to one other address is reached through that address, and its index
would refuse the browser, so [[present]] opens nothing and says why in
the banner.  That needs an address of the machine outside loopback;
the test takes the LAN address and is skipped on a machine without
one.

